    VALUES ('20th Anniversary: Brokeback Mountain', 'Sunday, June 22 at 7 PM Wednesday, June 25 at 4 & 7 PM “The whole movie is a rich, spacious, passionate way of showing, not telling, feelings that dare not speak their name and doing so with superb intelligence and magnificent candour.” — Peter Bradshaw, Guardian KPAC presents the 20th Anniversary screening of BROKEBACK MOUNTAIN. Set against the sweeping vistas of Wyoming and Texas, the film tells the story of two young men – a ranch-hand and a rodeo cowboy – who meet in the summer of 1963, and unexpectedly forge a lifelong connection, one whose complications, joys, and tragedies provide a testament to the endurance and power of love. A beautiful, epic Western, Brokeback Mountain''s love story is imbued with heartbreaking universality thanks to moving performances by Heath Ledger and Jake Gyllenhaal. Brokeback Mountain will also be part of our Movie Book Club partnership with BookPeople! Purchase the book at BookPeople and receive a free ticket to see the film at Kenworthy. Plus, enjoy 20% off the book if you see the film first and decide to read the book afterward. Join us and BookPeople for a book discussion before the film on Sunday, June 22 at 6:15 PM. Rated: R | 2 hr 14 min | Tickets: $8 Adult / Film Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/original-poster-web-204x300.jpg', 134, 'R', true)
    RETURNING id INTO v_movie_id;
