    VALUES ('Bans Off Moscow: Short Film Screening', 'Monday, March 3 at 7 PM Abortion Clinic Film Collective Series In the Abortion Clinic Film Collective series, we hear from medical directors and staff, mothers and daughters, criminal defense attorneys and advocates, about how their personal and professional lives have been affected post-Dobbs. Each portal provides a window into the broad and life-threatening ramifications of that Supreme Court decision and its devastating legacy for the health and well-being of our country and people. Illustrator, animator, and experimental filmmaker Ruth Hayes will be in attendance. Event hosted by the WSU Department of Digital Technology & Culture, WSU Program in Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies, Planned Parenthood Advocates of Greater Washington & Northern Idaho WSU Women*s Center, Bans Off Moscow, and the Vandal Film Club. PLEASE NOTE: The films in this series discuss pregnancy, abortion, miscarriages, and sexual violence. The content is geared towards an adult audience. Tickets: Free This event is a community rental and is not affiliated with the Kenworthy Performing Arts Centre.', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/Pink-Purple-Bold-Womens-Empowerment-Cinema-Club-Event-Flyer-232x300.jpg', 90, 'NR', true)
