    VALUES ('Come See Me in the Good Light', 'Saturday, March 7 at 7 PM “The film invites us to ask ourselves: What is poetry? How does it make meaning? Why does it offer solace like so few other art forms? All this ruminating takes place even as we are transfixed by Gibson and Falley.” — Lisa Kennedy, Variety KPAC presents the Academy Award–nominated documentary COME SEE ME IN THE GOOD LIGHT . Facing an incurable diagnosis, two poet lovers embark on a poignant yet unexpectedly humorous exploration of love, mortality, and life''s moments. Come See Me in the Good Light is an emotionally searing yet gently radiant portrait of Andrea Gibson and Megan Falley''s navigation of terminal illness that never loses sight of the warmth, humor, and love that defined their relationship. Sponsored by Jenn Duckworth, Palouse Sky Ranch and Stacy Pettitt and Holistic Connections, Mental Health Therapist. Rated: TV-MA | 1 hr 44 min | Tickets: $8 Adult / Film Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/CSM_Hero_-Laughter_Theatrical_DigitalPoster_1080x1600_wAcademy-203x300.png', 104, 'TV-MA', true)
