    VALUES ('Hitchcock Fest: The Birds', 'Wednesday, June 5 at 7 PM “Mr. Hitchcock and his associates have constructed a horror film that should raise the hackles of the most courageous and put goose-pimples on the toughest hide.” — Bosley Crowther, The New York Times KPAC presents THE BIRDS as part of their Hitchcock Fest series! A wealthy San Francisco socialite pursues a potential boyfriend to a small Northern California town that slowly takes a turn for the bizarre when birds of all kinds suddenly begin to attack people. Proving once again that build-up is the key to suspense, Alfred Hitchcock successfully turned birds into some of the most terrifying villains in horror history. When you see it on the big screen, you won''t be able to help yourself from ducking out of the way of the beaked terrors. Rated: PG-13 | 1 hr 59 min | Tickets: $8 Adult / Film Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/poster-107-196x300.jpg', 119, 'PG-13', true)
