    VALUES ('It&#8217;s Never Over, Jeff Buckley', 'Friday, August 22 at 7 PM Saturday, August 23 at 7 PM “It’s a deeply personal film, a life story told by the people who knew and loved Jeff. It hums with the emotion and vibrancy of Buckley’s music." — Brian Tallerico, RogerEbert.com KPAC presents the acclaimed music documentary, IT''S NEVER OVER, JEFF BUCKLEY. Jeff Buckley, a rising star with an otherworldly voice, left the 90s music world reeling when he died suddenly after the release of his debut album. In a tragic accident, Buckley drowned in the Wolf River in Memphis in 1997, leaving behind an unfinished second album and a legion of devastated family, friends and fans. Told through never-before-seen footage from Buckley’s archives, Oscar-nominated filmmaker Amy Berg crafts an illuminating portrait of one of modern music’s most influential and enigmatic figures. Magnolia Pictures will present 26 minutes of exclusive, never-before-seen, remastered footage from Jeff Buckley’s rare 1994 solo performance at The Middle East in Cambridge, MA. Stay after the film to see it. Rated: Not Rated | 1 hr 46 min | Tickets: $8 Adult / Film Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/poster-web-14-202x300.jpg', 26, 'N', true)
    RETURNING id INTO v_movie_id;
