    VALUES ('Janet Planet', 'Friday, August 9 at 7 PM Sunday, August 11 at 4 PM “Watching it feels eerily akin to running one’s fingers along a scar sustained in childhood and being magically projected back to the moment that injury was sustained..” — Peter Debruge, Variety KPAC presents JANET PLANET , the first feature film by Pulitzer Prize-winning playwright Annie Baker. In rural Western Massachusetts, 11-year-old Lacy spends the summer of 1991 at home, enthralled by her own imagination and the attention of her mother, Janet. As the months pass, three visitors enter their orbit, all captivated by Janet and her spellbinding nature. In her solitary moments, Lacy inhabits an inner world so extraordinarily detailed that it begins to seep into the outside world. Annie Baker captures a child''s experience of time passing, and the ineffability of a daughter falling out of love with her mother, in this singularly sublime film debut. Rated: PG-13 | 1 hr 53 min | Tickets: $8 Adult / Film Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/JanetPlanetKeyArtPoster.jpg', 113, 'PG-13', true)
