    VALUES ('KPAC Performing Arts Revue', 'Wednesday, May 1 at 6:30 PM Our special screening after the performances will be the animated classic THE BEAUTY AND THE BEAST! KPAC welcomes our essential partners in the performing arts to showcase a live revue on Wednesday, May 1 at 6:30 PM. Festival Dance troupe MOFE, APOD Theater, Moscow Community Theater (MCT), and WSU Stage all come together to perform an act that corresponds with a famous movie. MOFE will perform a dance sequence from An American in Paris; APOD will offer a sneak peak of their upcoming production of Beauty and the Beast; MCT will deliver a comedic scene from their most recent Harry Potter spoof Sally Cotter; and WSU Stage will sing one of the most beloved songs from Hamilton. A portion of all ticket sales will be donated to each company for Idaho Gives. Tickets are $12 for all ages. This event is part of KPAC’s Idaho Gives week of programming, celebrating our partnerships with local groups! Learn more about our goal to Pack the Kenworthy with donors. Tickets: $12 All Ages', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/kenworthypac_438795827_967168428744915_9038316061641139167_n-300x300.jpg', 90, 'NR', true)
