    VALUES ('Kinds of Kindness', 'Friday, July 26 at 7 PM Saturday, July 27 at 3 PM Sunday, July 28 at 7 PM “The fables are violently obscure, each stimulating an almost insatiable desire to put together the disparate pieces of these worlds. It is old-school Lanthimos, with stilted scenes and gelastic dialogue, brutally crashing into his heart-dropping punches.” — Maxwell Rabb, Chicago Reader KPAC presents KINDS OF KINDNESS , the new films from director Yorgos Lanthimos ( Poor Things, The Favourite ). A man seeks to break free from his predetermined path, a cop questions his wife''s demeanor after her return from a supposed drowning, and a woman searches for an extraordinary individual prophesied to become a renowned spiritual guide. A cold-hearted triptych brimming with caustic wit, Kinds of Kindness is Yorgos Lanthimos at his most misanthropic and bitingly funny. Rated: R | 2 hr 44 min | Tickets: $8 Adult / Film Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/KOK_PAYOFF_ONLINE_POSTER_1334x2000_US_FIN_web.jpg', 164, 'R', true)
