-- Met Live in HD: Grounded
DO $$
DECLARE v_movie_id UUID;
BEGIN
  SELECT id INTO v_movie_id FROM public.movies WHERE title = 'Met Live in HD: Grounded' LIMIT 1;
  IF v_movie_id IS NULL THEN
    INSERT INTO public.movies (title, description, poster_url, duration_minutes, rating, is_active)
    VALUES ('Met Live in HD: Grounded', 'Saturday, October 19 at 10 AM Two-time Tony Award–winning composer Jeanine Tesori’s powerful new opera Grounded, commissioned by the Met and based on librettist George Brant’s acclaimed play, wrestles with the ethical quandaries and psychological toll of 21st-century warfare. Mezzo-soprano Emily D’Angelo, one of opera’s most compelling young stars, portrays Jess, a hot-shot fighter pilot whose unplanned pregnancy takes her out of the cockpit and lands her in Las Vegas, operating a Reaper drone halfway around the world. As she struggles to adjust to this new way of doing battle, she fights to maintain her sanity, and her soul, as she is called to rain down death by remote control. Met Music Director Yannick Nézet-Séguin oversees the Met premiere of Tesori’s kaleidoscopic score and a cast that also features tenor Ben Bliss as the Wyoming rancher who becomes Jess’s husband. Michael Mayer’s high-tech staging, using a vast array of LED screens, presents a variety of perspectives on the action, including the drone’s predatory view from high above. Met Music Director Yannick Nézet-Séguin takes the podium to conduct Tesori’s kaleidoscopic opera, which will be transmitted live from the Met stage to cinemas on October 19. Run Time: 2 hr 44 min | Tickets: $20 Adult / $15 Student / Met Live in HD Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/Grounded-Individual-Web-Thumbnail-1000x1480-1.jpg', 164, 'NR', true)
