    VALUES ('Moscow Film Society: Mulholland Drive', 'Thursday, October 6 at 7 PM "One of the very few movies in which the pieces not only add up to much more than the whole, but also supersede it with a series of (for the most part) fascinating fragments." — Observer Moscow Film Society presents MULHOLLAND DRIVE as part of their Cronenberg vs Lynch series. After a car wreck on the winding Mulholland Drive renders a woman amnesiac, she and a perky Hollywood-hopeful search for clues and answers across Los Angeles in a twisting venture beyond dreams and reality. David Lynch creates a world of waking dreams and nightmares that washes over the audience leaving them breathlessly captivated by what they just witnessed. One of the greatest films of the aughts and of all time, MULHOLLAND DRIVE, will twist its way into your psyche leaving you to endlessly contemplate its images, sounds and meanings. The film must be experienced like a dream so join us in a dark room where you are consumed by the images and sounds of a master director at work. Rated: R | 2 hr 27 min | Tickets: $5 General Admission', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/MulhollandDrivePoster-198x300.jpg', 147, 'R', true)
