    VALUES ('National Theatre Live: Life of Pi', 'Saturday, January 3 at 3 PM "It will make you believe in theatre. A triumph ★★★★" — Sunday Times KPAC presents the National Theatre Live production of LIFE OF PI . Puppetry, magic and storytelling combine in a unique, Olivier Award-winning stage adaptation of the best-selling novel. After a cargo ship sinks in the middle of the vast Pacific Ocean, a 16-year-old boy named Pi is stranded on a lifeboat with four other survivors – a hyena, a zebra, an orangutan and a Royal Bengal tiger. Time is against them, nature is harsh, who will survive? Filmed live in London’s West End and featuring state-of-the-art visuals, the epic journey of endurance and hope is bought to life in a breath-taking new way for cinemas screens. Rated: PG | 2 hr 30 min | Tickets: $10 General Admission / No Film Passes', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/NTL-Life-of-Pi-Listing-Image-Portrait-874x1240px-211x300.jpg', 150, 'PG', true)
