    VALUES ('Palouse Cult Film Revival: To Wong Foo, Thanks for Everything! Julie Newmar', 'Tuesday, September 5 at 7:00 PM “Imagine, "Wong Foo" suggests, a world where people stopped judging one another and simply surrendered to the silliness that''s dormant inside us.” — San Francisco Chronicle Palouse Cult Film Revival and Moscow Human Rights Commission present TO WONG FOO, THANKS FOR EVERYTHING! JULIE NEWMAR ! Three drag queens travel cross-country until their car breaks down, leaving them stranded in a small town. TO WONG FOO is a groundbreaking film that was ahead of its time in celebrating the beauty and art of drag culture. It balances campy fun with heartfelt moments and is led by three fantastic performances from Wesley Snipes, Patrick Swayze and John Leguizamo. This is a free screening hosted by Moscow Human Rights Commission in celebration of Moscow Inclusive Community Month! Rated: PG-13 | 1 hr 49 min | Tickets: Free', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/poster-3-200x300.jpg', 109, 'PG-13', true)
