    VALUES ('Relighting Ceremony: Sunset Boulevard', 'Sunday, September 21 Relighting Ceremony at 7 PM Film Screening at 8 PM KPAC celebrates the restoration of our historic marquee with a free screening of SUNSET BOULEVARD ! Join us for a ribbon-cutting ceremony and community photo under the lights at 7 PM. Director Colin Mannex will welcome the entire community on Main Street for this public commemoration of our shared history. Sunset Boulevard will screen at 8 PM. A screenwriter develops a dangerous relationship with a faded film star determined to make a triumphant return. Arguably the greatest movie about Hollywood, Billy Wilder''s masterpiece Sunset Boulevard is a tremendously entertaining combination of noir, black comedy, and character study. Sponsored by Palouse Sky Ranch – Cheryl and Donna and the Classic Films Committee. Major support for Marquee Restoration from Idaho Heritage Trust & National Parks Service, M.J. Murdock Charitable Trust and Innovia Foundation. Rated: Approved | 1 hr 50 min | Tickets: Free', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/Relighting-Ceremony-27x41-web-198x300.jpg', 110, 'A', true)
