BEGIN
  SELECT id INTO v_movie_id FROM public.movies WHERE title = 'Science on Screen: Arrival' LIMIT 1;
  IF v_movie_id IS NULL THEN
    INSERT INTO public.movies (title, description, poster_url, duration_minutes, rating, is_active)
    VALUES ('Science on Screen: Arrival', 'Tuesday, March 24 at 7 PM KPAC and U of I Department of Politics and Philosophy presents ARRIVAL as part of our Science on Screen® series, showcasing films with introductions by notable figures from the world of science, technology, and medicine. Arrival delivers a must-see experience for fans of thinking person''s sci-fi that anchors its heady themes with genuinely affecting emotion and a terrific performance from Amy Adams. LANGUAGE, TIME, AND THE LIMITS OF CONTROL Bryce Blankenship, Senior Instructor of Philosophy at University of Idaho , will discuss how our measurements and language shape the way we perceive reality. Are we bound by a linear view of time, or can we imagine it as something more interconnected and fluid? This talk will explore Arrival and its ideas about language, perception, free will, and the illusion of control, inviting audiences to consider how expanding our ways of thinking might expand our experience of the world. An initiative of the COOLIDGE CORNER THEATRE, with major support from the ALFRED P. SLOAN FOUNDATION. Sponsored by University of Idaho Department of Politics and Philosophy. Rated: PG-13 | 1 hr 56 min | Tickets: $8 Adult / Free for U of I Students / Film Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/poster-56-192x300.webp', 116, 'PG-13', true)
