    VALUES ('The Boy and the Heron', 'December 8-21 “No one needed further proof that he’s a master. This meditation on grief and growing up does solidify the position, however, that Miyazaki remains the greatest living animator today, period.” — Rolling Stone KPAC presents Hayao Miyazaki''s final film THE BOY AND THE HERON . A young boy named Mahito yearning for his mother ventures into a world shared by the living and the dead. There, death comes to an end, and life finds a new beginning. A semi-autobiographical fantasy from the mind of Hayao Miyazaki. Soulfully exploring thought-provoking themes through a beautifully animated lens, The Boy and the Heron is another Miyazaki masterpiece. Please note which version of the film is screening for each showtime. English Dubbed ( Dec. 20 at 1 PM) Japanese with English Subtitles (Dec. 21 at 4 PM) English Dubbed Sensory Friendly (Dec. 19 at 4 PM) Rated: PG-13 | 2 hr 4 min | Tickets: $8 Adult or $5 Child or Film Pass', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/poster-web-3-205x300.jpg', 124, 'PG-13', true)
