    VALUES ('The Neighborhood Theatre: Our Town', 'Monday, May 4 at 7 PM The Neighborhood Theatre presents a staged reading of OUR TOWN. First produced and published in 1938, this Pulitzer Prize–winning drama of life in the small village of Grover’s Corners has become an American classic and is Thornton Wilder’s most renowned and most frequently performed play. Through the everyday moments of two neighboring families, the play follows love, marriage, and loss, offering a quietly profound reflection on the beauty and brevity of human existence. This event is part of KPAC’s Idaho Gives week of programming! Learn more about our goal to Pack the Kenworthy with donors. Tickets: $12 Adult / $5 Student & Child', 'https://www.kenworthy.org/wp-content/uploads/Our-Town-Poster-web-225x300.jpg', 90, 'NR', true)
